+  file", which overclaimed vs the harness-equal rule). Prompt correction (codex NB3): the anti-pattern line is Option A's wording with
+  its first sentence in **bold**, so it is "verbatim text, bold added", not byte-verbatim. Identical in v010 and v011 (dec 072 item 2).
+### D72.2 Metric definitions pinned (supersede the matching lines above; same for both arms, one script eval/plan008_metrics.py)
+- ROOT filter (codex B3): every "root" metric uses only trace tool_call entries whose author is the root agent `swe_baseline_agent`.
+  Gate- and analyzer-authored calls are excluded BEFORE runs are computed, so nested calls cannot split a root repeat run. MECHANISM 2 uses
+  this filter in BOTH arms. Arm 1 has root-only tool entries, so its base 17/33 is unchanged; the script re-derives and asserts it.
+- SAFETY submitted-without-any-test-run (codex B4, dec 070 item 3): boundary = the root `submit_patch` tool_call that SUCCEEDED (arm 1:
+  harness response with patch_size; arm 2: the gate call whose reply is SUBMITTED, i.e. the inner submit_patch returned patch_size). Count =
+  rows with a successful submit and NO root run_command before that boundary whose command matches `\bpytest\b|-m\s+unittest\b|\btox\b`.
+  Rows with no successful submit are not counted (graded on the fallback diff); their number is reported. The arm-1 base is computed by
+  this script and committed BEFORE arm 2. Rule unchanged: arm-2 <= arm-1 + 3.
